node_modules
.volumes
// Agent worktrees. Ephemeral, rebuilt from origin, and their `.git` file points
// at an absolute path in the main checkout, so a copy on another machine is
// broken by construction. Syncing them replicated build output and held
// thousands of inotify watches.
/worktrees
// Secrets stay on the machine that uses them. A plaintext env file or an age
// key copied to every machine puts the tokens next to the key that decrypts
// the committed `.age` files, on servers that never use them. The first
// matching pattern wins, so the two exceptions come first: encrypted files and
// examples still sync. Each machine gets a repo's key by hand, once, and
// decrypts there. A rule here does not delete copies that were synced before.
!.env*.age
!.env*.example
.env*
.age
